<title>USA: Basic Petroleum says truckers on strike.</title>
<headline>Basic Petroleum says truckers on strike.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basic Petroleum International Ltd said Monday that drivers employed by the company's supplier of trucking services have initiated a strike and that oil shipments by truck on the La Libertad-Raxruja road have been partially interrupted.</p>
<p>The company said the strikers' action has also caused a partial suspension of work on Basic's third pipeline, which runs from La Libertad to Raxruja.</p>
<p>None of the drivers on strike are employed by Basic, the company said.  </p>
<p>A company spokesman, in a telephone interview, declined to speculate how much the strike has or will cost the company.</p>
<p>The company said it is currently engaged in discussions with Guatemalan government officials and representatives of the drivers on strike.</p>
</text>
